    "created_at": "2020-04-17T05:53:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-17T05:53:05Z",
    "body": "> a very-light-yellow background that, when hovered over, has a little popup saying \"Authoring requirement ([?](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/introduction.html#how-to-read-this-specification))\" or something.\r\n\r\nI agree that’d be a useful way to style it.\r\n\r\nAs far as “very-light” for the color, we might want to ask page in some people with accessibility domain knowledge and get them to weigh in with guidance around best practices on cases like this. I can imagine that for some readers, some backgrounds would be too light for them to be able to distinguish from a completely-white background.\r\n\r\nMaybe there are some color-analyzer tools for checking this — as there are such tools for what’s sort of the opposite (and more-common) case of checking backgrounds to make sure they aren’t too dark to the point of not providing enough contrast).",
