    "created_at": "2020-04-17T10:34:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-04-17T10:34:58Z",
    "body": "I thought that a light yellow background might not work well with \"night shift\" warmer color setting, but I tested in macOS and it seemed ok for `rgb(255, 245, 220)`.\r\n\r\nHere's a quick mockup with preceding text \"Applies only to web developers:\" in italic, and light yellow background.\r\n<img width=\"1108\" alt=\"Screenshot of `sizes` and `as` attribute definitions.\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/244772/79559953-edc10d80-80a6-11ea-8b01-94f18824d98e.png\">\r\n\r\nThe CSS I used here is\r\n```css\r\nspan.author {\r\n    background: rgb(255, 245, 220);\r\n    padding: 0.25em 0;\r\n}\r\nspan.author::before {\r\n    content: \"Applies only to web developers: \";\r\n    font-style: italic;\r\n}\r\n```\r\nAlthough CSS generated content is exposed in the accessibility tree, it wouldn't be available without CSS. Where the annotation ends is also only conveyed with color.",
